WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.767
- [Steve] Anna, nice to finally meet you.

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.212
- Nice to meet you guys.

00:00:03.212 --> 00:00:04.045
- Nice to see-
- How are you?

00:00:04.045 --> 00:00:06.115
- I'm so good, how are you?
- Thanks for having us.

00:00:06.115 --> 00:00:07.198
- Oh no, I'm very excited.

00:00:07.198 --> 00:00:08.129
I'm really excited about stealing

00:00:08.129 --> 00:00:09.687
that leather jacket my man.

00:00:09.687 --> 00:00:10.523
(audience laughs)

00:00:10.523 --> 00:00:12.126
Did you watch "The Sopranos"?

00:00:12.126 --> 00:00:12.959
Were you under "The Sopranos" there?

00:00:12.959 --> 00:00:14.547
- Oh, I would watch "The
Sopranos" with my dad.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:16.566
- Oh, I love that.
- So I like

00:00:16.566 --> 00:00:18.461
couldn't quote you like
everything from every episode,

00:00:18.461 --> 00:00:20.199
but like that was like a bonding thing.

00:00:20.199 --> 00:00:21.583
Just like-
- That's cool.

00:00:21.583 --> 00:00:23.120
- Murder but also family dynamics.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.007
(all laughing)
(Kelly clapping)

00:00:24.007 --> 00:00:25.333
- That was the show was about.
- Exactly.

00:00:25.333 --> 00:00:26.391
- Interpersonal relationships.

00:00:26.391 --> 00:00:27.224
- [Michael] Exactly.
- That's what

00:00:27.224 --> 00:00:28.057
the show is about.

00:00:28.057 --> 00:00:28.890
(audience applauding)
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:30.484
- I love you so much.

00:00:30.484 --> 00:00:31.935
(laughs) Murder.

00:00:31.935 --> 00:00:33.093
- Its true.
- Family dynamics,

00:00:33.093 --> 00:00:34.185
you're so funny.

00:00:34.185 --> 00:00:36.626
Okay, so you guys did the show together

00:00:36.626 --> 00:00:38.211
for five seasons, right?

00:00:38.211 --> 00:00:39.901
So what were your first
impressions of each other?

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.267
Did you like each other at first,

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:42.795
or were you like, hmm?

00:00:42.795 --> 00:00:43.879
- We don't like each other now.

00:00:43.879 --> 00:00:45.140
(all laughing)
- Now.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:45.973
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:00:45.973 --> 00:00:47.217
- I mean, at first.

00:00:47.217 --> 00:00:50.655
- Well, you know, Michael was there first,

00:00:50.655 --> 00:00:52.109
and I came on in the second season

00:00:52.109 --> 00:00:55.121
so he was one of the leads of the show.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.581
So it was one of my first days,

00:00:56.581 --> 00:00:58.426
I was very excited to meet him, you know?

00:00:58.426 --> 00:00:59.259
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:00.092
- And they introduced us

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:02.265
and he went, "Yeah, how are you doing?"

00:01:02.265 --> 00:01:03.415
He gave me the fish hand,

00:01:03.415 --> 00:01:04.279
you know the fish hand?

00:01:04.279 --> 00:01:05.873
- Yeah.
- This is what he gave me.

00:01:05.873 --> 00:01:06.706
- [Kelly] Yeah, I'll never-

00:01:06.706 --> 00:01:07.539
- He gave me the fish hand and-

00:01:07.539 --> 00:01:08.804
- [Kelly] I'll never
see you again (laughs).

00:01:08.804 --> 00:01:09.637
- That's exactly right.

00:01:09.637 --> 00:01:12.062
The pay no mind list and
that's exactly what he did,

00:01:12.062 --> 00:01:14.494
and to this day it's kinda the same way.

00:01:14.494 --> 00:01:16.442
(all laughing)

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:19.692
- Kelly, I was told to keep a distance.

00:01:20.556 --> 00:01:23.641
He had a terrible reputation
coming out of Las Vegas

00:01:23.641 --> 00:01:26.046
as being very difficult and-

00:01:26.046 --> 00:01:26.879
- [Kelly] Is this true?

00:01:26.879 --> 00:01:28.840
- It took a while to get used to his ways,

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:30.010
his demands and everything.

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:30.843
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:01:30.843 --> 00:01:32.450
- And then we wind up
one night, he came over,

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.024
he said, "Let's go out for a drink,"

00:01:35.024 --> 00:01:37.797
and that was one of thousands of drinks.

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:41.302
But just to show you what
things are like even today,

00:01:41.302 --> 00:01:43.394
this is what happened today,

00:01:43.394 --> 00:01:44.352
- We were on site.
- Trying to get

00:01:44.352 --> 00:01:45.185
into the front gate.

00:01:45.185 --> 00:01:46.018
Michael, Schirepa,

00:01:46.018 --> 00:01:46.851
- Mamashu...

00:01:46.851 --> 00:01:47.684
Oh, yeah.

00:01:47.684 --> 00:01:49.170
- Michael, Schirepa, they
can't even get my name right.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:50.837
- [Kelly] They can't even
spell your name right (laughs).

00:01:50.837 --> 00:01:52.362
- Because he's always pulling

00:01:52.362 --> 00:01:55.214
these moves on me, there you go.

00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:56.951
- (laughs) That's awesome.
- I didn't do anything

00:01:56.951 --> 00:01:58.285
that's the way cards fall, Kelly.

00:01:58.285 --> 00:01:59.802
- Those are my favorite friendships,

00:01:59.802 --> 00:02:02.213
the ones where you can call
each other out constantly,

00:02:02.213 --> 00:02:03.046
I love that.

00:02:03.046 --> 00:02:05.502
Well, in your first scene,
in the first episode,

00:02:05.502 --> 00:02:07.635
you're driving, you were driving, right?

00:02:07.635 --> 00:02:10.193
So is it true that you
didn't know how to drive?

00:02:10.193 --> 00:02:11.276
- No.

00:02:11.276 --> 00:02:13.859
I spent my adulthood in New York City

00:02:13.859 --> 00:02:16.094
so a lot of us don't drive,

00:02:16.094 --> 00:02:19.888
but I got cast basically to
be Tony Soprano's driver.

00:02:19.888 --> 00:02:21.011
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:02:21.011 --> 00:02:22.143
So I didn't tell them that

00:02:22.143 --> 00:02:23.151
'cause I wanted the...

00:02:23.151 --> 00:02:24.205
You do whatever you can

00:02:24.205 --> 00:02:25.202
to get a job, right?
- Yeah, to get a job.

00:02:25.202 --> 00:02:26.035
- Oh my god!
- I was like, yeah,

00:02:26.035 --> 00:02:26.868
I can drive.

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:27.725
I'm thinking, how hard
could it be it's a TV show?

00:02:27.725 --> 00:02:29.437
- [Kelly] Actors are liars, okay.

00:02:29.437 --> 00:02:30.270
- Actors are liars.

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:31.226
- Yes, okay.

00:02:31.226 --> 00:02:32.059
- [Michael] Exactly.

00:02:32.059 --> 00:02:34.311
- So I figured they're
gonna block off the streets,

00:02:34.311 --> 00:02:35.144
it's gonna be fine.

00:02:35.144 --> 00:02:38.063
But I had to drive
backwards down the sidewalk

00:02:38.063 --> 00:02:39.879
with trees on both sides,

00:02:39.879 --> 00:02:44.353
doing dialogue to Tony
Soprano, James Gandolfini.

00:02:44.353 --> 00:02:46.406
And I did it like five times,

00:02:46.406 --> 00:02:48.027
and then the director said,

00:02:48.027 --> 00:02:50.727
"Do it one more time, twice
as far, twice as fast."

00:02:50.727 --> 00:02:51.756
Boom!

00:02:51.756 --> 00:02:53.805
Right into a tree, backed right into it,

00:02:53.805 --> 00:02:55.979
destroyed the rear end of the car.

00:02:55.979 --> 00:02:59.115
Airbags go off, James
Gandolfini's head snaps,

00:02:59.115 --> 00:03:00.665
there's smoke, people are running

00:03:00.665 --> 00:03:03.999
and I'm just like, "I'm getting fired.

00:03:03.999 --> 00:03:05.271
There's no way they're keeping me.

00:03:05.271 --> 00:03:07.219
He's the star of the show, he's..."

00:03:07.219 --> 00:03:09.583
And then I look over,
- What is he saying?

00:03:09.583 --> 00:03:11.712
- He just starts losing
it, laughing hysterically.

00:03:11.712 --> 00:03:12.545
(Anna gasps)
(audience laughing)

00:03:12.545 --> 00:03:14.322
- Oh, I was kind of what
kind of losing it (laughs).

00:03:14.322 --> 00:03:15.155
(audience clapping)

00:03:15.155 --> 00:03:17.224
- Hysterically laughing and I was like,

00:03:17.224 --> 00:03:19.142
- Oh my god!
- "All right, it's gonna

00:03:19.142 --> 00:03:19.975
be okay."

00:03:19.975 --> 00:03:21.585
- Okay, you can still
have your driver's license

00:03:21.585 --> 00:03:23.039
for a while and still
do something like that.

00:03:23.039 --> 00:03:24.075
I mean, not that I've done that

00:03:24.075 --> 00:03:25.545
in like a Target parking lot or anything,

00:03:25.545 --> 00:03:27.039
but...
(all laughing)

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:28.452
It was years ago, whatever.

00:03:28.452 --> 00:03:29.905
Tell us about the new book.

00:03:29.905 --> 00:03:31.370
So why did you wanna do this?

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:34.045
What's the reason for wanting to do this?

00:03:34.045 --> 00:03:35.488
- Well, we were doing a podcast-

00:03:35.488 --> 00:03:37.654
- [Kelly] I know that, yeah.
- At the start of the pandemic

00:03:37.654 --> 00:03:39.719
and we were bringing on all the actors,

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:42.391
all the writers, directors, crew people,

00:03:42.391 --> 00:03:43.891
and, we were like,

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:45.743
we have to...

00:03:45.743 --> 00:03:48.187
It's like 300 hours this
podcast is gonna be,

00:03:48.187 --> 00:03:49.299
but we wanted to find something

00:03:49.299 --> 00:03:51.396
that would be more condensed.

00:03:51.396 --> 00:03:53.859
We went back and interviewed
people to get more stories

00:03:53.859 --> 00:03:56.366
'cause there was a lot we
didn't put on the podcast,

00:03:56.366 --> 00:03:57.545
and this is an oral history.

00:03:57.545 --> 00:03:59.511
It's from the mouths of
the people who made it.

00:03:59.511 --> 00:04:02.449
So this is firsthand behind
the scenes information.

00:04:02.449 --> 00:04:03.722
- It's so cool.
(audience clapping)

00:04:03.722 --> 00:04:07.295
- Including the creator David Chase

00:04:07.295 --> 00:04:08.966
and 98% of the cast,

00:04:08.966 --> 00:04:10.777
so if you're a "Soprano" fan,

00:04:10.777 --> 00:04:11.777
you're gonna want this book, it's good.

00:04:11.777 --> 00:04:13.171
- Well you need to be living under a rock

00:04:13.171 --> 00:04:14.148
not really to be a fan.

00:04:14.148 --> 00:04:15.902
So that's why I think
it's so cool that you...

00:04:15.902 --> 00:04:18.405
It's an amazing thing to
be a part of something

00:04:18.405 --> 00:04:21.417
so magical, like such a big
huge thing of pop culture.

00:04:21.417 --> 00:04:23.144
Like did that set in right away for y'all

00:04:23.144 --> 00:04:25.207
or did it take like a few seasons?

00:04:25.207 --> 00:04:26.893
- No, no, it did not set in.

00:04:26.893 --> 00:04:30.127
I mean, we weren't sure if it
was even gonna work as a show,

00:04:30.127 --> 00:04:32.359
'cause it had not been any real series

00:04:32.359 --> 00:04:35.371
on cable that were hits at the time.

00:04:35.371 --> 00:04:36.937
And when it came out though,

00:04:36.937 --> 00:04:39.835
it got these crazy reviews
all over the place,

00:04:39.835 --> 00:04:43.140
and then it started to get a following,

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:44.357
and there were billboards,

00:04:44.357 --> 00:04:45.375
and that kind of thing,

00:04:45.375 --> 00:04:46.933
and it just kept going from there.

00:04:46.933 --> 00:04:49.013
Now it seems like it's more popular

00:04:49.013 --> 00:04:50.088
than it ever was.

00:04:50.088 --> 00:04:50.921
- Yeah.

00:04:50.921 --> 00:04:51.754
- And that's amazing

00:04:51.754 --> 00:04:52.587
to be a part of-
- Amazing.

00:04:52.587 --> 00:04:53.420
- Something that huge.

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:55.448
- I think 50 years from now,

00:04:55.448 --> 00:04:56.913
they'll still be watching this thing.

00:04:56.913 --> 00:04:58.326
- I know, well, that's

00:04:58.326 --> 00:04:59.561
a sign of a classic.

00:04:59.561 --> 00:05:00.994
Well, the show famously ended

00:05:00.994 --> 00:05:03.439
in the middle of a scene and a song.

00:05:03.439 --> 00:05:06.126
No one knows if Tony
Soprano lived or died,

00:05:06.126 --> 00:05:07.912
so what do you think?

00:05:07.912 --> 00:05:10.899
- [Steve] I think Tony
Soprano is alive and well,

00:05:10.899 --> 00:05:12.870
and eating onion rings in New Jersey.

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:13.756
(audience cheering)
(Anna laughs)

00:05:13.756 --> 00:05:15.214
- [Kelly] I think that sounds awesome.

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:16.289
- That's what I think.

00:05:16.289 --> 00:05:17.122
- Okay.

00:05:17.122 --> 00:05:17.955
(audience clapping)

00:05:17.955 --> 00:05:20.301
I have a feeling you have a
different opinion (laughs).

00:05:20.301 --> 00:05:22.249
- Of course, he always
got a different opinion.

00:05:22.249 --> 00:05:24.246
- I saw him, he did the thinking man pose.

00:05:24.246 --> 00:05:25.374
- Yeah.
- No.

00:05:25.374 --> 00:05:28.689
I think the cut to black
was his point of view,

00:05:28.689 --> 00:05:31.909
and that's end for the character.

00:05:31.909 --> 00:05:33.201
That was the last thing he saw

00:05:33.201 --> 00:05:34.939
and then it was snuffed out.
- Very (indistinct).

00:05:34.939 --> 00:05:36.165
- And Michael is wrong Kelly.

00:05:36.165 --> 00:05:37.570
(all laughing)

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:39.908
Listen to uncle Steve, Michael's wrong.

